1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe d'Auvergne, Duc de Bouillon
2 CONT Spymaster, Scientist, Writer and Sailor
2 CONT
2 CONT From < [https://www.westminster-abbey.org/abbey-commemorations/commemorations/philippe-dauvergne-duc-de-bouillon Westminster Abbey] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Vice Admiral Philippe d'Auvergne, Royal Navy, fellow of the Royal Society, was buried in the churchyard of St Margaret's Westminster on 22nd September 1816 but he has no marker or memorial.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in St Helier on the island of Jersey and baptised in 1754. His parents were Charles, army officer, and his first wife Elizabeth (Le Geyt). He had several half brothers including Corbet who died in 1825 in Paris. While 
2 CONC serving in the Royal Navy he sailed on an Arctic expedition and was present at the battle of Bunker Hill during the American War of Independence. He was acquitted at a court martial for the loss of his ship off the coast. While se
2 CONC rving in another ship he was captured by the French and imprisoned in Brittany where he met Charles d'Auvergne, duke of Bouillon. On his release he sailed to an island off the coast of Brazil and was again acquitted for the loss o
2 CONC f a ship. He also went to India. While convalescing in France the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Godefroy_de_La_Tour_d%27Auvergne  Duke of Bouillon] adopted him as his son.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Napoleonic wars he was commodore for the defence of the Channel Islands. He served as a spymaster for the British on the coasts of France. By 1803 he had taken the title of Duke of Bouillon. In 1810 he was promoted a Vi
2 CONC ce Admiral. He wrote a book about sea compasses. He had at least three illegitimate children - son Philippe died while in the Royal Navy, Mary married Sir (later Admiral) Henry Prescott and Anne married Admiral John Aplin. He died
2 CONC  in debt in Parliament Street at Holmes Hotel on 18th September.
2 CONT
2 CONT Further reading:
2 CONT The tragedy of Philippe D'Auvergne by G.R. Balleine, 1973 < [https://books.google.com/books?id=NFwDAAAAMAAJ GoogleBooks] > 
2 CONT Oxford Dictionary of National Biography
2 CONT OCCUPATION
2 CONT Spymaster; scientist; writer; sailor
2 CONT LOCATION
2 CONT St Margaret's Church
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # https://morethannelson.com/officer/philippe-dauvergne/
2 CONT # https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippe_d%27Auvergne
2 CONT # https://www.westminster-abbey.org/abbey-commemorations/commemorations/philippe-dauvergne-duc-de-bouillon
2 CONT # https://www.britishmuseum.org/collection/term/BIOG52134
2 CONT # “The Adoption of Philip Dauvergne” < [https://www.heraldica.org/topics/france/bouillon.htm#adoption link] > (In another, more plausible version of the story, the genealogical researches were started only after this first meeting
2 CONC  and miraculously found the connection between the families...). 
