2 CONT ==Senator in French government==
2 CONT ''~• from [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georges_Washington_de_La_Fayette wikipedia]''<br/>
2 CONT Oscar Thomas Gilbert Motier de La Fayette (1815–1881) was educated at the École Polytechnique and served as an artillery officer in Algeria. He entered the Chamber of Deputies in 1846 and voted, like his father, with the extreme L
2 CONC eft. After the revolution of 1848, he received a post in the provisional government; as a member of the Constituent Assembly, he became secretary of the war committee. After the dissolution of the Legislative Assembly in 1851, he 
2 CONC retired from public life, but emerged on the establishment of the third republic, becoming a life senator in 1875."
