1 NAME D. Afonso /de Bragança/ 5.º Duque de Lafões
2 GIVN D. Afonso
2 NSFX 5.º Duque de Lafões
2 _MARNM de Bragança
1 NAME Afonso de Bragança, 5º duque de Lafões
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 19 MAR 1893
1 DEAT
2 DATE 22 SEP 1946
2 PLAC São Martinho do Porto
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Portugal
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 2º Duque de Miranda do Corvo. 11.º Conde de Miranda do Corvo. 5.º Duque de Lafões. 2.º Duques de Miranda do Corvo. 8.º Marquês de Arronches.
2 CONT
2 CONT The title Duque de Lafões was created on 17-2-1718 for Dom Pedro Henrique de Bragança Sousa Tavares Mascarenhas da Silva, nephew of King João V of Portugal, being the son of Dom Miguel de Bragança, illegitimate son of King Pedro I
2 CONC I. Although the title has passed two times through the female line, the present dukes still descend in the male line from the Portuguese royal family, and because of that are members of the dynasty Capet, with as eldest certain an
2 CONC cestor Robert le Fort, margrave of Neustria (+ 866), probably a descendant through the counts of Hesbaye of another Robert who was dux in Neustria between 654-677. Dom Pedro de Portugal e Castro (1830-1878) who married the 4.Duque
2 CONC sa de Lafões, is a descendant of Afonso 1.Duque de Bragança (1377-1461), illegitimate son of King João I of Portugal.  The title Duque de Miranda do Corvo was created on 13-5-1796 for a son of the 2.Duque de Lafões, and was given 
2 CONC in 1920 to the 5.Duque de Lafões.
2 CONT
2 CONT in, http://heirsofeurope.blogspot.pt/2010/02/lafoes.html
