1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jean Maurice Paul Jules de Noailles, 6th Duke of Ayen was the son of Adrien de Noailles, 8th Duke of Noailles and a member of the French Resistance in World War II.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the French Resistance, arrested by the Gestapo on 22 January 1942 as a result of an anonymous denunciation. He was tortured and interned at the Paris Gestapo headquarters on Avenue Foch and then in Compiègne, an
2 CONC d then deported successively to Buchenwald, Flossenburg, Oranienburg, and finally Bergen-Belsen, where he died a few days before the end of the war. In 1952, the Paris military court sentenced Suzanne Provost, a Gestapo collaborat
2 CONC or accused of having denounced Jean de Noailles, to twenty years of imprisonment.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://man8rove.com/fr/profile/trqz5sbg-jean-de-noailles
2 CONT
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/pierfit?lang=en&p=jean&n=de+noailles
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean_Maurice_Paul_Jules_de_Noailles
